condary_5"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Describing Future Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Simple Future has two different forms in English: \"will\" and \"be going to.\" You use the present continuous tense to talk about something planned.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">FORM <span class=\"italic\">Will</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> to suggest someone is going to do something voluntarily. It can also be used to make a prediction or promise.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[<span class=\"italic\">will</span> + verb]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Sally will meet up with Vanessa later.<br/>I'll call you when I get to the restaurant.<br/>Peter will be the first person in line at the buffet.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">FORM <span class=\"italic\">Be Going To</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">going to</span> to express an intention.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[<span class=\"italic\">am</span> / <span class=\"italic\">is</span> / <span class=\"italic\">are</span> + <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> + verb]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Sally is going to meet up with her friends after work.<br/>Leonard is going to be the next Vice-President.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you  talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[<span class=\"italic\">am</span> / <span class=\"italic\">is</span> / <span class=\"italic\">are</span> + present participle]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Are you thinking about having your friends over for dinner this week?</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pantry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small room in a house in which food is stored", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I store all my food in the pantry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you would hear in conversation between two friends at home.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "everything except the kitchen sink", "type": "name"}, {"content": "almost anything a person can think of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I brought everything except for the kitchen sink.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "perishable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not likely to stay fresh for a long time if not eaten or used", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The food in this bag is perishable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "air-conditioning", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a system used for cooling and drying the air in a building or room", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The air-conditioning in my car wasn't working.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to accompany", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be included with something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll include a little paragraph to accompany the photos.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to soak up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enjoy feeling or experiencing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The other half was spent soaking up the sun on my patio.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to surf", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look or search for information using the Internet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I spent half of my morning surfing the Internet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "patio", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a flat area of ground, usually behind a house", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa was soaking up the sun on her patio.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_